Imports:
  - Types:
      - GRDBDatabaseStorageAdapter
    From: SignalServiceKit/Storage/Database

Usages:
  single_writer_many_readers: |
    The app has exactly one database file and one facade instance over it. All reads and
    writes throughout the entire codebase — sync, async, and awaitable — funnel through this
    one facade's transaction-opening methods rather than opening connections independently.
  change_observation: |
    Certain mutations (thread/interaction/story-message "touches" and id-mapping updates) are
    reported to a change observer as part of the same write, so UI layers can react to what
    changed without polling.

Annotations: |
  This cell is the single database transaction facade used throughout the app: every read or
  write of persisted state, of any kind, ultimately goes through one of this cell's transaction
  methods.
  Use `single_writer_many_readers` for `SDSDatabaseStorage`'s role.
  Use `change_observation` for the touch/id-mapping methods.

---

"SDSDatabaseStorage(databaseFileUrl: String)":
  location: SDSDatabaseStorage.swift
  annotations: |
    The app's single database facade, wrapping a `GRDBDatabaseStorageAdapter` connection pool.

    `databaseFileUrl`: location of the encrypted database file on disk

    Use `single_writer_many_readers` for why every subsystem depends on this one type.
    Use `GRDBDatabaseStorageAdapter` from Imports as the underlying connection pool this
    facade wraps.
  properties:
    "databaseFileUrl -> String": |
      Location of the on-disk database file.
    "grdbStorage -> String": |
      The underlying `GRDBDatabaseStorageAdapter` connection pool this facade delegates to.
  methods:
    "read(block: DBReadTransaction) -> result: String": |
      Opens a read transaction and runs `block` inside it, returning its result.
    "write(block: DBWriteTransaction) -> result: String": |
      Opens a write transaction, runs `block` inside it, commits, and returns its result.
    "asyncWrite(block: DBWriteTransaction)": |
      Schedules `block` to run inside a write transaction asynchronously, without blocking
      the caller.
    "awaitableWrite(block: DBWriteTransaction) -> result: String": |
      Runs `block` inside a write transaction and suspends the calling task until it commits.
    "touch(threadUniqueId: String, shouldReindex: Bool, tx: DBWriteTransaction)": |
      Marks a thread as changed for UI/search purposes without altering its stored columns.

      Use `change_observation` for how this reaches the UI layer.
    "logFileSizes()": |
      Logs the current database, WAL, and SHM file sizes for diagnostics.

---

